00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:37.680
and I think this is where it gets back to what we're saying —

405
00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:40.840
you need a sort of tool to manage

406
00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:44.640
all of this, because skills can vary — it depends which model you're using.

407
00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:46.160
It depends exactly what context it's in.

408
00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:48.080
Like, everything is context dependent.

409
00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:51.000
And this is why every skill is unique.

410
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:54.520
And every model that activates those skills is like —

411
00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:55.640
they're different from one another.

412
00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:01.360
So if you are an avid Hermes agent person,

413
00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:04.840
then you might want to make sure that it works well for you.

414
00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:07.400
Because I don't know — I'm a Claude fan or whatever.

