00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:58.080
and looking into what the optimization should look like, it's now overwritten

432
00:22:58.760 --> 00:23:02.520
the first skill, showing what's changed.

433
00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:06.360
And yeah, without too much surprise,

434
00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:09.360
the front matter has been changed.

435
00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:10.360
I wouldn't be surprised

436
00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:14.200
if there's a bit of reduction as well in terms of sizing.

437
00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:17.760
Yeah.

438
00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:19.480
But maybe —

439
00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:23.200
just maybe — isn't that instead a problem of skills

440
00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:26.320
and language contexts and all that — isn't

441
00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:29.320
that just a problem of

442
00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:31.960
personal

443
00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:36.480
bad judgment in how to put directives to someone else?

444
00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:41.120
If you have a proper system with how-to-dos

